# Decompiled proprietary game code; regenerable via ilspycmd
decompiled/

# DLLs copied from the game install; proprietary and regenerable
bibites-mod/libs/

# Build output
bibites-mod/bin/
bibites-mod/obj/
bin/

# The graphical launcher's Win32 resource object: the Common Controls 6 manifest
# and the application icon, compiled by `go generate ./cmd/multiverse-launcher-gui`
# (see go/cmd/multiverse-launcher-gui/generate.go) from the checked-in manifest
# and release/kit/bibites-multiverse.ico. It is build output, which
# release/tracked-binaries.txt does not allow this repository to track, and it is
# byte-for-byte reproducible from those two inputs. It is IGNORED rather than
# merely untracked on purpose: `go build -buildvcs=true` reads `git status`, and
# an untracked file there would stamp every release binary vcs.modified=true.
go/cmd/multiverse-launcher-gui/*.syso

# The hosting kit's cross-compiled artifacts. deploy/ship.sh builds the relay,
# the archive and ringstat for linux/amd64 and linux/arm64 here and scps them to
# the instance; they are regenerable from go/ and are ~60 MB a set.
deploy/stage/

# AWS cloud-world build and migration staging. The runtime bundle and manifest are
# reproducible; the game archive is third-party payload; imported saves are the
# user's worlds; join files contain live credentials. None belongs in Git.
cloud/aws/dist/
cloud/aws/imports/
cloud/aws/private/

# E2E rig runtime state. e2e/data/ holds the sidecar journals — the durable custody
# record of decision D2 — which belong to one run of one machine, never to the repo.
e2e/data/
e2e/logs/
e2e/logs-m3/
e2e/relay-data/
e2e/archive-data/
e2e/run/

# The LAN rig's logs (slot 2 is on the second computer)
e2e/logs-m3-lan/

# The M4 six-slot rig's runtime state. e2e/data-m4/slot-1 is a COPY of the T1
# journal made by `run-m4.sh arm`; the ORIGINAL is the only copy of the resume
# test's input and is never deleted. Both rigs were retired and compressed on
# 2026-08-08 (see e2e/*.tar.zst below): the original now lives at
# data/slot-1/journal/journal.log inside e2e/data.tar.zst, and the copy inside
# e2e/data-m4.tar.zst. Extract before re-running the resume test. The trailing
# slash on e2e/run-m4/ keeps e2e/run-m4.sh itself tracked.
e2e/data-m4/
e2e/logs-m4/
e2e/relay-data-m4/
e2e/archive-data-m4/
e2e/run-m4/

# The M4 LAN rig's runtime state. Slot 6 runs on the second computer, so only five
# journals are ever here. It gets its OWN relay data dir rather than sharing the
# rehearsal's: run-m4.sh phase 5 spliced a seventh peer into e2e/relay-data-m4/
# and left that map 4x2, and a reservation never shrinks a map.
e2e/data-m4-lan/
e2e/logs-m4-lan/
e2e/relay-data-m4-lan/
e2e/archive-data-m4-lan/
e2e/run-m4-lan/

# The species-guard regression check's evidence: BepInEx log copies from the three
# throwaway instances species-guard-check.sh runs.
e2e/logs-m5-guard/

# The relay's TLS material for contract-b/4.0 (contract-b-m4.md §22, B23), minted
# by e2e/crossing/mint-tls.sh. It holds the CA's PRIVATE KEY and the server's, and
# nothing under it may ever be committed — a private key that reaches the index is
# a key that has to be rotated, and rotating THIS CA costs a trust import on the
# second computer that D9 forbids this machine to perform. `ca.crt` is the only
# file in there that leaves this machine, and it travels by hand beside the
# bundle, exactly as the token used to.
#
# The per-peer CREDENTIALS of §22 B22 are not here at all: like ~/.multiverse-token
# before them, they live outside the repository, in ~/.multiverse/, one 0600 file
# per identity. `<relay-data-dir>/peers.json` — the verifier store — is already
# covered by the e2e/relay-data*/ rules above.
e2e/tls-m4-lan/
e2e/tls-*/

# Key material and captured secrets wherever they land, because the rule above
# only works while somebody remembers to put them in the right directory. There
# is nothing of these shapes tracked in this repository and there never should be;
# `git add -f` is the escape hatch if a fixture ever legitimately needs one.
*.key
*.pem
*.p12
*.pfx
*.secret

# The live rig's observation loop. e2e/baselines/ is otherwise TRACKED — the
# committed baseline captures under it are evidence of runs that finished — but
# m4-collector/ is a running loop, not a capture: it copies five world saves and
# one /api/status sample every 5 minutes, for as long as the deployment is up.
# That is 0.5 GB/day, and at 2026-08-08 it already held 343 MB in 1,148 files.
# It is excluded so no `git add -A` can turn a continuous writer into repository
# history. Prune it and commit a keeper by explicit path if a sample is worth
# keeping; `git add -f` is the escape hatch.
e2e/baselines/m4-collector/

# Retired rigs, parked as tar.zst in place of the directories above. A retired
# runtime dir is still the record of a run that happened, so it is compressed
# rather than deleted — but it is runtime state either way and never enters the
# repo. Restore one with `tar --zstd -xf e2e/<name>.tar.zst -C e2e/`.
e2e/*.tar.zst
